    {
      "id": "opl_nau_ch13_regression_02",
      "answer": "The means are $\\bar x=3$ and $\\bar y=7.4$. Also,\n\n$$S_{xx}=\\sum(x_i-\\bar x)^2=10,$$\n\n$$S_{xy}=\\sum(x_i-\\bar x)(y_i-\\bar y)=19.$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$b_1=\\frac{S_{xy}}{S_{xx}}=1.9,$$\n\n$$b_0=\\bar y-b_1\\bar x=7.4-1.9(3)=1.7.$$\n\na. The least-squares line is\n\n$$\\hat y=1.7+1.9x.$$\n\nb. Pearson's correlation is\n\n$$r=\\frac{S_{xy}}{\\sqrt{S_{xx}S_{yy}}}\\approx0.9851,$$\n\nindicating a very strong positive linear association.\n\nc. At $x=6$,\n\n$$\\hat y=1.7+1.9(6)=13.1.$$",
